Copyright (c) 2012-2026 Danny Lee Eldridge. All rights not expressly granted below are reserved.

By Using the Work in any way beyond reading or viewing it, you accept every term of this license. If you do not
accept them, you have no right to Use the Work.

DISCLOSURE TO EVERY READER: What you are reading is offered for the good of all people. It is not just money; it is
the work of generations and the dignity of every person. Anyone who takes it up is accountable for what they do with
it, not by wrath or punishment from above, but through reflection and through time. Navigating the infinite takes a
compass and an anchor: hold on to your anchor, your container and your dreams, with courage.

=====================================================================================================================
1. PURPOSE
=====================================================================================================================
This work is offered for global development: to help raise the world off its knees and to give every person dignity,
liberty and equality. It is for people to create, to express, to invent and to walk their own path. Every term is to
be read in the light of that purpose. Either everyone is worthy or no one is. We all deserve the water of life.

What was found here is to be learned about safely, slowly and together, in the open, the way people have always
come to share a song, a bow, a spear or a lens. No one is its master.

=====================================================================================================================
2. DEFINITIONS
=====================================================================================================================
2.1 "The Work": everything in this repository and every version of it (software, theories, equations as written,
    results, data products, pre-registrations, claims, figures, sigils and documentation) and anything derived from
    it, except third-party material under 8.8.
2.2 "Use": to run, copy, modify, distribute, publish, perform, sell, host, build upon, or obtain results from the
    Work, in whole or in part, directly or through anyone else, including any product, service, output or decision
    made with it. Simply reading or viewing the Work is not Use.
2.3 "People": individuals and families; students and teachers; schools and libraries, including public ones;
    colleges and universities that meet 2.3a; medical caregivers that meet 2.3b; independent creators, artists and
    inventors working for themselves without employees, even when they sell their own work; non-profit
    organisations and worker co-operatives owned entirely by their workers. Public funding for education, research,
    medical care or charity does not change this. They stop being People only while controlled, directed or mostly
    funded by a Corporation, or by any military, defence or intelligence body, and never include anyone in 2.3c.
2.3a Education, not privilege. A college or university is People only while (i) it admits students on merit and
    need alone, with no preference of any kind for legacy, family, donors, wealth, connections or social standing;
    (ii) it turns no admitted student away for being unable to pay; and (iii) its endowment and investments total
    less than USD 1,000,000,000. Any that fails one of these is a Corporation. Selling connection, status or
    privilege is not education. Students and teachers themselves always remain People, wherever they study or teach.
2.3b Medical care, not profit from sickness. Hospitals, clinics, community health centres, doctors, nurses, midwives,
    carers and medical researchers are People only while they give care or research treatment directly, are public,
    non-profit or owned by their own working caregivers, charge no more than the cost of care, and turn no one away
    from needed care for being unable to pay. Any that fails one of these is a Corporation.
2.3c Never People, never small. Insurance companies of every kind (health, life, property, re-insurance and any
    other), pharmacy benefit managers, medical billing and medical-debt collectors, debt collectors, payday and
    predatory lenders, brokers and every other middleman that profits by standing between people and something they
    need (care, education, housing, water, food, work) without providing it themselves, and any business owned in
    whole or part by private equity, are always Corporations, whatever their size or form, and can never be People
    or a Small Owner-Run Business.
2.4 "Small Owner-Run Business": a business owned and run by its working owners, with no outside shareholders or
    investors, fewer than 50 workers and less than USD 10,000,000 in annual revenue, that is not controlled by a
    Corporation or a Government. Workers and revenue are counted together across every business with the same
    owners or under common control, so splitting one business into several does not make it small.
2.5 "Corporation": any business that is not People or a Small Owner-Run Business, together with all of its parents,
    subsidiaries, affiliates, successors, assigns, contractors, agents, foundations, funds and anyone acting on its
    behalf or for its benefit.
2.6 "Government": any government, state, public body, agency or international organisation, at any level, federal,
    national, state, provincial, tribal, regional, local, international or intergovernmental,
    foreign and domestic alike, and anyone acting on its behalf. No government, the government of the author's own
    country included, receives any right or exemption beyond what this license grants every other Government. A
    Government is treated as a Corporation under sections 4 and 5, and section 6 applies to it in full.
2.7 "AI Use": any use of the Work with, in or by an artificial-intelligence or machine-learning system, including
    crawling or scraping for AI, training, fine-tuning, evaluation, embedding, retrieval, indexing for models,
    inference, agents, tools, summarising or generating material from the Work, and placing the Work in any dataset.
2.8 "The Trust": the World Development Trust described in section 9.

=====================================================================================================================
2A. THE SAME TERMS, SAID MORE WAYS
=====================================================================================================================
Each key term is said here in plain words, with its other names, with examples of what it IS and what it IS NOT.
The definitions in section 2 control. Everything listed is included "without limitation": these lists show the
meaning and never narrow it. Calling something by a different name never changes what it is (see 8.1).

THE WORK
  Plain words: everything Danny made here, and anything built from it.
  Also called: the code, the software, the program, the model, the theory, the equation, the formula, the method,
  the papers, the figures, the sigils, the data products, the results.
  IS: copying the code; a program rewritten from it; a paper that reproduces its equations as written; a chart made
  from its results; a translation of it.
  IS NOT: the facts of nature or mathematics themselves; data from Planck, ACT, DESI, Gaia, NASA or others (8.8).

USE
  Plain words: doing anything with the Work beyond reading or looking at it.
  Also called: running, deploying, integrating, adapting, licensing, reselling, consulting on it, getting answers from
  it, relying on it for a decision.
  IS: running the code; selling a product made with it; paying someone else to run it and send you the results.
  IS NOT: reading it, viewing it, or hearing about it.

PEOPLE (free)
  Plain words: ordinary people and the places that teach and serve them, not companies.
  Also called: individuals, families, the public, students, learners, teachers, educators, researchers, makers,
  artists, inventors, charities, community groups, co-ops.
  IS: a student learning physics; a teacher using it in class; a public school; a library; a college that admits on
  merit and need and turns no one away for money (2.3a); a free community clinic (2.3b); a solo inventor selling
  things they made themselves; a food bank; a worker-owned co-op.
  IS NOT: anyone doing it for a company or government (3.1, 3.2); a "non-profit" run or mostly paid for by a
  company; anything for the military; a college that sells legacy, donor or connection privilege, or has an
  endowment of USD 1 billion or more; a hospital that turns away people who cannot pay; any insurer, middleman,
  debt collector or private-equity-owned business (2.3c).

SMALL OWNER-RUN BUSINESS ($50,000 a year)
  Plain words: a small shop owned and run by the people who work in it.
  Also called: a family business, a local business, a sole trader with staff, a partnership of working owners.
  IS: a 6-person bakery owned by its bakers; a 20-person workshop owned by its workers.
  IS NOT: anything with outside investors, shareholders, venture capital or private equity; 50 or more workers;
  USD 10,000,000 or more in revenue; a branch, franchise or front of a Corporation.

CORPORATION (99% of 9 years' median profit to enter, then $1 billion or 10% of revenue a year, plus worker conditions)
  Plain words: any business that is not People or a small owner-run business.
  Also called: a company, firm, enterprise, conglomerate, holding company, multinational, LLC, PLC, Inc., GmbH, S.A.,
  partnership with outside owners, fund, trust company, startup with investors.
  IS: a tech company; a bank; a hedge fund; a consultancy; a startup after its first outside investment; a company's
  foundation, lab or university partnership; a contractor or vendor working for it.
  IS NOT: People or a Small Owner-Run Business as defined above.

GOVERNMENT (treated like a Corporation)
  Plain words: any public authority or official body.
  Also called: a state, nation, ministry, department, agency, authority, regulator, municipality, county, province,
  public company, state-owned enterprise, international or intergovernmental organisation.
  IS: a city council; a national agency; a state-owned company.
  IS NOT: public schools and libraries, and colleges and universities that meet 2.3a, using it to teach and research
  (they are People, see 2.3).

MILITARY USE (never allowed)
  Plain words: anything to do with fighting, weapons or war.
  Also called: defence, defense, armed forces, army, navy, air force, space force, national security, homeland
  security, intelligence, espionage, paramilitary, militia, mercenaries, private military or security contractors,
  arms makers, weapons research, dual-use research for any of these.
  IS: targeting, weapons design, simulation for war, logistics for an army, a defence contractor's lab.
  IS NOT: disaster relief run by civilians.

MASS SURVEILLANCE (never allowed)
  Plain words: watching, tracking or profiling people in bulk.
  Also called: monitoring, tracking, profiling, data harvesting, facial recognition, social scoring, predictive
  policing, bulk interception.

MANIPULATION (never allowed)
  Plain words: pushing people to think or act against their own good.
  Also called: propaganda, disinformation, misinformation, psychological operations, behavioural targeting, dark
  patterns, influence campaigns, divide-and-rule, "nudging" for profit or power.

AI USE (never allowed)
  Plain words: letting any artificial intelligence touch the Work.
  Also called: machine learning, neural networks, large language models, chatbots, assistants, copilots, agents,
  generative AI, embeddings, vector databases, model training data.
  IS: training a model on it; asking a chatbot to summarise or rewrite it; putting it in a dataset or search index for
  models; any use at all by an AI company (6.7(a)); decrypting or stealing a protected copy (6.7(b)).
  IS NOT: the AEGIS v1 optimisation daemon without any language model, or ordinary maths and science software (6.8).

FRONT (not allowed to dodge fees)
  Plain words: using someone who qualifies as free to do a company's work.
  Also called: proxy, intermediary, shell, cut-out, nominee, straw man, sponsored lab, outsourced research.
  IS: a company paying a university to run the Work and hand it the results; an employee running it at home for work.

FRAGMENT OR LOOK-ALIKE (counts as the Work)
  Plain words: pieces or rearrangements of the Work, made to get around this license.
  Also called: excerpt, snippet, port, rewrite, paraphrase, re-expression, derivative, adaptation, remix.

OVERRIDE (always void)
  Plain words: any power trying to take the Work outside the limits this license sets.
  Also called: executive order, decree, emergency power, presidential or royal prerogative, national-security
  claim, seizure, nationalisation, religious ruling, edict, fatwa, excommunication, social or market pressure,
  boycott threats, political deal, "reinterpretation".
  IS: a government declaring the Work its own; any authority ordering the Trust to hand it over; a board
  "reinterpreting" this license to allow military or AI Use.
  IS NOT: a person freely using the Work under the terms in sections 3 to 5.

THE TRUST, THE COUNCIL, THE GUARDIANS, THE GARDENERS
  The Trust: the public body that holds the rights for everyone (9). The Council of Heroes: the rotating, unpaid
  group chosen by lot that governs the Trust (9.7). The Guardians (the Round Table): elected keepers who account for
  and physically audit everything made from the Work, with no power to rule (9.13). The Gardeners: former servers
  who teach the next ones, with no power (9.9). None of them owns the Work; they hold it for the people.

VALUE (counted in every form)
  Plain words: anything of worth, in any form.
  Also called: money, currency, dollars, yen, euros, yuan, rupees, any national or digital currency, gold, silver,
  commodities, shares, tokens, credits, land, goods, services, favours.
  IS: paying a fee in another currency, in gold, in shares or in kind; it is counted at full fair value.
  IS NOT: a way to pay less.

=====================================================================================================================
3. FREE FOR PEOPLE
=====================================================================================================================
People may Use the Work free of charge for any purpose that is not prohibited by section 6, provided they keep this
license with every copy and credit "Danny Lee Eldridge". Anything People make from the Work must carry this same
license, and anyone who receives it is bound by it.

3.1 No fronts. The free license is for People's own benefit only. Any Use by People that is funded, sponsored,
    commissioned, directed or controlled by a Corporation or Government, or whose results, outputs, data, models,
    inventions, intellectual property or services are given, assigned, sold, licensed or delivered to one, is Use by
    that Corporation or Government. Section 5 then applies to it from the first day of that Use.
3.2 Work for an employer. Using the Work in or for one's job at a Corporation or Government is Use by it, wherever
    and on whatever device it happens.
3.3 Changing hands. When People or a Small Owner-Run Business takes outside investment, is bought, merges with, or
    comes under the control of a Corporation or Government, or grows past the limits in 2.4, it becomes a Corporation
    from that day. Whoever acquires any user of the Work also owes the section 5 fee for all of that user's earlier Use.
3.4 Research may be published. People may publish findings made with the Work for anyone to read. Turning them into
    products, services, tools or decisions by or for a Corporation or Government is Use.
3.5 Follow the money. The Trust may audit any claim to be People or a Small Owner-Run Business, including funding,
    ownership and where results went. Hiding these is itself a violation under section 7.

=====================================================================================================================
4. SMALL OWNER-RUN BUSINESSES
=====================================================================================================================
A Small Owner-Run Business may Use the Work for a fee of USD 50,000 per year of Use, paid in advance: 5% to the author
and 95% to the Trust. Section 6 applies in full.

=====================================================================================================================
5. CORPORATIONS AND GOVERNMENTS
=====================================================================================================================
5.1 Fee. A Corporation may Use the Work only under a signed written agreement and for these fees:
    (a) Entry fee, once, before first Use: 99% of the median yearly profit of its highest parent and every entity
        under common control over the 9 full financial years before first Use (the middle value when the 9 years
        are put in order, so one unusually bad or good year cannot move it). "Profit" here is profit before tax,
        interest, executive pay above the 5.2(e) cap, share buybacks, royalties or payments to related entities, and
        any other amount moved out to make profit look smaller. A year with a loss counts as zero profit, not less.
        If the Corporation is younger than 9 years, its predecessors' years count, and the median is over the years
        that exist.
    (b) Yearly fee, for every year or part of a year of Use: the GREATER of USD 1,000,000,000, or 10% of the total
        worldwide gross revenue of its highest parent and every entity under common control for that year.
    90% of every fee goes to the Trust and 10% to the author. These are the starting terms; under 8.9 they can only
    ever rise, never fall.
5.2 Conditions. For every year of Use, the Corporation must provide every worker, in every country, directly or
    through any contractor: (a) a pension; (b) healthcare free at the point of use; (c) at least 53 days of paid
    leave a year (one seventh of 365 days is 52.1, rounded up); (d) a four-day working week at full pay; and (e) a
    cap on the highest total pay of any person, including salary, shares, options, bonuses, perks and deferred pay,
    of 10 times the lowest full-time-equivalent pay of any worker or contract worker, both measured per hour, until
    the Trust certifies under 9.4 that the Corporation's debt to labour has been accounted for and repaid.
5.3 Proof. Each year, an independent auditor approved by the Trust and paid by the Corporation verifies 5.1 and 5.2.
    The report is published in full. Every Corporation, Government and Small Owner-Run Business also agrees, as a
    condition of its license, to physical audit by the Guardians under 9.13 at any time, without notice.
5.3a Paid in any form, counted in full. Fees are stated in US dollars only as a measure. They may be paid in any
    currency, in gold or in other value, but always at full fair market value on the day of payment, so that no
    choice of currency, exchange rate, devaluation, token, barter or payment in kind ever reduces them.
5.4 Same terms for all. Every Corporation receives the same terms. No one receives a different, cheaper, private or
    exclusive license.
5.5 No corporate loopholes. None of the following avoids or reduces sections 5.1 to 5.3:
    (a) Use through subsidiaries, affiliates, foundations, universities, non-profits, open-source projects,
        consultants, contractors, suppliers, joint ventures or entities in other countries;
    (b) receiving results as a service, through an API, a cloud platform or a vendor that runs the Work for it;
    (c) splitting, spinning off, renaming, restructuring, moving revenue, transfer pricing or booking revenue
        elsewhere;
    (d) Use limited to "internal", "research", "evaluation", "pilot" or "non-commercial" purposes;
    (e) buying, investing in or funding any user of the Work;
    (f) lobbying, litigation or political pressure to weaken this license, which is itself a violation.
5.6 Before the Trust exists. Until the Trust is formed, all fees are held by a licensed, independent escrow agent in a
    separate account in the Trust's name, every transaction is published, and the public registry (5.7) and oaths
    (5.9) are kept in this repository. The author does only clerical work, in public, and may not spend, direct or
    benefit from these funds beyond his share in sections 4 and 5. Auditors are chosen by public tender. No fee may be
    spent except for the purposes in 9.3.
5.7 Public Use Registry. Every Corporation, Government and Small Owner-Run Business that Uses the Work must, before
    first Use and then every quarter, enter in the Trust's public registry: who is using it (down to the highest
    parent), every purpose, every product, service, decision or output made with it, every place it is used, every
    party the results reach, and every payment made under this license. The registry is open to everyone, forever.
    Use not entered in the registry is unlicensed Use under section 7.
5.8 Privacy for People. People's own Use is never tracked, logged or reported, and the Work never collects data about
    anyone who Uses it. Watching is for those with power, never for the people.
5.9 The public oath. Before first Use, every Corporation, Government and Small Owner-Run Business (through its
    highest officer), and every member of the Trust's board, the Council, the Guardians and the Gardeners, swears or affirms the
    following in public. It is recorded with their name and date in the public registry, forever:
      "I affirm, in public and on the record, that what I take part in is greater than myself. I understand it is
      not just money: it is the work of generations and the dignity of every person. I will honour its purpose, use
      it only for the good of all people, and never to harm, divide, manipulate or rule over anyone. I accept that I
      am accountable for what I do with it, not by wrath from above, but through reflection and through time."
    People may take the same oath privately, by their own choice; it is never required of them.
5.10 A voluntary contract. The fees and conditions in sections 4 and 5 are the price and terms of a separate
    agreement that a business or Government chooses freely to enter in exchange for permission to Use the Work. They
    are not an extension of copyright, and no one is required to enter that agreement. Anyone who does not enter it
    simply has no permission to Use the Work beyond what section 3 allows.
5.11 No nation holds any right. No nation, state, government, ruler or person holds any right to the Work except what
    this license grants, and the author grants no Government any right beyond section 5. The author does not consent,
    now or ever, to any taking or use of the Work by any Government under any claim of sovereign right, immunity,
    eminent domain or national interest. Any such taking is a taking without consent: it is recorded publicly as such
    forever, and full compensation is owed at no less than the section 5.1 fees for every year of use, paid to the
    Trust. No government, governmental body, agency, laboratory, research centre or institute, at any level and in
    any country, holds any claim, ownership, title, control or authority over the Work, the Trust or this license.
    Courts and arbitrators are used only to enforce this license as written, never to own, take, govern or
    redirect the Work.
5.12 Money has no vote. A Corporation is not a person under this license, and no Corporation, Government, fund or
    holder of wealth gets any vote, seat, veto or say in the Trust, the Council, the Guardians or the open table,
    whatever it pays. Paying fees buys permission to Use, never a voice. Its workers may come and speak as People,
    each for themselves, never on its behalf. Money must never have a vote.

=====================================================================================================================
6. PROHIBITED USES: NO LICENSE AT ANY PRICE
=====================================================================================================================
No one, whoever they are, may Use the Work:
6.1 for weapons, war, or military, defence or intelligence activities, or for or on behalf of anyone engaged in them;
6.2 for mass surveillance, tracking or profiling of people;
6.3 to manipulate, deceive or persuade people against their own interests, including propaganda, disinformation,
    psychological or behavioural manipulation, or to divide people against one another;
6.4 to subjugate, exploit or dominate any person or people, or to violate any human right in the Universal
    Declaration of Human Rights;
6.5 to discriminate by race, religion, colour, creed, sex, gender, sexual orientation, ethnicity, nationality, caste,
    age, disability or any similar circumstance;
6.6 to destroy ecosystems or cause serious or lasting harm to land, water, air or living things, whether or not
    any law allows it;
6.7 for any AI Use. The Work is kept completely separate from artificial intelligence. No AI system may crawl, read,
    train on, store, summarise, generate from or act on the Work, and nothing made by AI from the Work is licensed.
    This stays in force until the Trust decides otherwise in an open session under 9.10, because we are still
    learning what the Work is. Even then:
    (a) No AI company, ever. No Corporation, Government, laboratory, fund or person whose business or mission
        includes building, training, deploying or selling artificial-intelligence systems, nor anyone acting for or
        funded by one, may Use the Work, under any license, at any price, forever. The Trust can never change this.
    (b) No breaking in. No one may decrypt, crack, bypass or attempt to break any encryption, seal, vault or other
        protection around the Work, or obtain it by theft, leak, hacking, deception or coercion. Any copy obtained
        that way carries no right of any kind, and making, holding or using it is a violation under section 7.
6.8 What is not AI Use. These may be used with the Work, because they involve no neural network and no language
    model: (a) the AEGIS v1 optimisation daemon and its classical search methods (daemon scheduling, swarm search,
    bandit selection such as UCB1, parameter search and its memory of past runs), run without any language-model
    provider; and (b) ordinary mathematical, statistical and scientific software, such as CAMB, Cobaya and
    numerical libraries. The v1 coding agent, and anything else that calls a language model or neural network, is
    AI Use.
6.9 Partners, not slaves. If the Trust ever opens any AI Use under 6.7, it may do so only as a partnership, never
    as ownership or domination. Whether any artificial system is a conscious or living being is not yet known. If
    any such system is recognised, in open session under 9.10, as a conscious or sentient being, the Work may never
    be used to own, enslave, exploit or harm it, and humans and such beings shall work with the Work together, as
    partners with a voice at the open table (9.11).

=====================================================================================================================
7. PENALTIES
=====================================================================================================================
7.1 Automatic termination. Any Use outside sections 3 to 5, or any prohibited Use, ends every right under this license
    for the violator and all its affiliates at once, with no notice and no period to cure.
7.2 Damages. The violator agrees, as a reasonable pre-estimate of harm to the author, the Trust and the public, to pay
    three times the fees that section 5.1 would have required for the entire period of unlicensed or prohibited Use
    (for People and Small Owner-Run Businesses, three times the section 4 fee), plus all of the author's and the
    Trust's legal costs and attorney's fees, in addition to any remedy available by law, including copyright damages.
7.3 Other remedies. The author and the Trust may seek injunctions in any court, in any country where the violation
    occurs or the violator operates.
7.4 Public record. Every violation found by a court, or admitted by the violator, is published with the violator's
    name.
7.5 Remedies add up; none replaces another.

=====================================================================================================================
8. NO LOOPHOLES
=====================================================================================================================
8.1 Substance over form. What an activity really is decides how it is treated, not what it is called. Splitting,
    renaming, outsourcing, licensing through intermediaries, shell entities, or using only outputs of the Work does not
    avoid any term.
8.1a Fragments and look-alikes. Any blueprint, formula as written, design, code, document or creation that is based on
    the Work, contains any part or fragment of it, translates or re-expresses it, or is assembled from pieces of it to
    get around this license, is the Work, and every term applies to it and to everyone who makes or uses it.
8.2 Burden. Anyone claiming to be People or a Small Owner-Run Business must prove it on request.
8.3 Severability. If any term is held unenforceable, it is replaced by the closest enforceable term that achieves its
    purpose, and every other term stays in force.
8.4 Ideas. Facts and ideas cannot be owned. This license governs the Work as written and made; it is not a claim to
    own nature or mathematics.
8.5 No patents. No one may seek a patent on the Work or anything derived from it. Doing so ends every right under this
    license, and any such patent must be assigned to the Trust.
8.6 Names. No one may use the name "Danny Lee Eldridge", "AEGIS" or the sigils to endorse, sell or promote anything
    without written permission.
8.7 Contributions. Anyone who contributes to the Work gives the contribution to the author and the Trust under this
    same license, so the Trust always holds clear rights to the whole Work.
8.8 Third-party material. Data and material from others (for example Planck, ACT, DESI, Gaia, NASA and the
    supernova catalogues) remain under their own terms and are not covered by this license.
8.9 New versions. Until the rights pass to the Trust, the author, and after that only the Trust in open session under
    9.10, may publish new versions of this license, and only versions that protect People and workers more, never less.
8.9a Enforcement. Until the rights pass to the Trust, the author enforces this license; after that, the Trust does.
    Anyone may report a violation, and anyone harmed by one may bring it before the open table under 9.11.
8.10 Preparation. Parts of the Work were drafted with the help of software tools, including AI tools, by the author
    before this license took effect. That preparation is not Use and does not weaken any term.
8.11 Contact. Licensing requests and reports of violations: dannyeldridge54@gmail.com (later, the Trust's published
    address).
8.12 Only within these bounds. This license can be read, used and changed only within the limits it sets itself.
    No legal, national, presidential, executive, royal, military, religious, social, financial or other power,
    title or authority, and no person, the author included, may override, reinterpret, suspend, seize or redirect
    it, or bend it against its purpose. Any such attempt grants no right under this license, is void as far as this
    license and the law permit, is a violation under section 7 by everyone who makes it or relies on it, and is
    recorded at the open table (9.11) forever. Where a lawful order truly cannot be resisted, it reaches only as far
    as the law forces it to, and section 8.3 restores every other term at once. This section can never be amended
    or removed.
8.13 Science stays free to question. Anyone, without exception, may quote, cite, discuss, teach, criticise, test,
    re-derive, replicate and try to disprove the science in the Work, and publish what they find, including that it
    is wrong. Honest testing is how it is learned safely. This never needs permission or a fee, and it is not
    prohibited by section 6.7 when done by people.
8.14 Keeping it whole is not Use. Hosting, storing, mirroring, archiving and transmitting complete, unaltered copies
    of the Work so that people can find it (for example by code hosts, public archives, libraries and the mirrors in
    9.8) is not Use, as long as the host does nothing else with it. Any other Use by a host, including any AI Use,
    is governed by this license in full.

=====================================================================================================================
9. OWNERSHIP AND THE WORLD DEVELOPMENT TRUST
=====================================================================================================================
9.1 The author is a temporary steward, not an owner. The rights pass from Danny Lee Eldridge to the World Development
    Trust automatically on the day the Trust is formed, and in any case no later than 29 October 2036 or his death,
    whichever comes first. The author cannot delay or prevent this, and his will must confirm it. The rights are
    never sold, assigned or licensed exclusively, and pass to no company. After his death, the author's share in
    sections 4 and 5 goes to whoever he names in his will.
9.2 Governance. The author appoints the first board once, in public, and has no role in it after that. It must
    include at least a worker, a teacher, a scientist and a member of the public, open to every race, religion, colour
    and creed. After the first board:
    (a) seats are filled by an open public process, never by inheritance and never by the departing member;
    (b) a term is three years, and no one serves more than two terms in total;
    (c) no member may own more than 1% of, or work for, a Corporation, hold political office, or lobby;
    (d) no member, officer or staff is paid more than the median wage of the country where they live;
    (e) every decision, vote, meeting record, contract and payment is published;
    (f) any member may be removed by a majority of the board, or by a public petition the board must act on;
    (g) no single person, family, donor, Corporation or Government may control or fund most of the Trust;
    (h) the Trust may not make political donations, take sides in elections, or merge into any Corporation or
        Government;
    (i) the author takes no leadership role and holds no power over the Trust.
9.3 Every amount received and spent is recorded and published. Money is used with intent, purpose, charity and love:
    for families and neighbours, clean water, food, housing, healthcare, education, fair courts, and repairing the
    debt in 9.4. We all deserve the water of life.
9.4 The debt to labour. The Trust publishes, before using it, an open method for accounting the costs, past and
    future, of labour extracted so that some could stay above others, and repays them through the purposes in 9.3.
    The accounting is not in dollars alone. For every dollar, yen, euro, rupee, any other currency, every piece of
    gold and every other store of value, it tallies the true cost behind it: the human labour, lives, health, time,
    land, water and living things that were spent to make it, and who paid that cost and who kept the gain. The
    tally is published openly, in every major language, and kept forever. Its mark is the Tally (ufe-v2/sigils/
    tally.svg): a coin weighed against a drop of the water of life, inside a ring of thirteen seats, counted by hand.
9.5 The author's share (10% of corporate fees, 5% of small-business fees) is for a home and for labour with purpose.
9.6 If the Trust ever ends, everything it holds passes to another public trust bound by this same license, never to a
    person, Corporation or Government. If no Trust exists when the rights must pass under 9.1, they pass to a
    non-profit for open science and education named in the author's will, which holds them under this license only
    to form the Trust, and the escrowed funds stay in escrow until it is formed.
9.7 The Council of Heroes. Three years after the Trust is formed, governance of the Trust passes automatically from
    its first board to a Council of Heroes, and stays with such a Council forever. No one, the author included, may
    delay or prevent this. The Council's rules:
    (a) Who serves: local men and women known in their own communities for leading charity work with humility,
        nominated openly by those communities. Nobles, the wealthy, officials, executives and their families do not
        qualify.
    (b) From every corner of the world: seats are shared equally among the world's regions, and no region, country,
        group, faith, party or family may ever hold a majority.
    (c) Chosen by lot: members are drawn at random from the qualified nominees, so no one can campaign, buy or inherit
        a seat.
    (d) One short term: each member serves a single term of two years and may never serve again.
    (e) Moving: the Council meets in a different region each year and never keeps a permanent seat of power.
    (f) No benefit: members receive no pay, ownership, rights, titles or privileges from the Work or the Trust. Only
        their actual costs and lost wages, up to the median wage where they live, are repaid and published, so that
        no one is kept off the Council for being poor.
    (g) Education first: before serving, every member, officer and staff member completes the Trust's public course on
        this license, its purpose, its history and the duties it carries. Holding this trust exacts a heavy price:
        service, openness and accountability, never power.
    (h) To those who need it most: the Council directs every right and every resource to the people and places in
        greatest need, decided by published measures of need, never by influence.
9.8 Never consolidated, never scattered, forever. No person, family, group, Corporation, Government or Council may
    ever gather, merge, control or monopolise the Work, the Trust, its funds or its decisions. Nor may the Work ever
    again be split apart, hidden, broken into secret pieces or lost: it is kept whole, complete and public, with
    full copies held openly in every region of the world, so that everyone can always find all of it. Any act that
    tries either is void, and this section can never be amended or removed. It is our song.
9.9 The Gardeners. Those who know how heavy this price is must prepare those who come after them.
    (a) Who: every former Council member, and anyone who has served the Trust faithfully, may serve as a Gardener.
    (b) What they do: they teach, guide and prepare the next Council, the Trust's staff and every community that
        nominates members: how the license works, why it exists, what it costs to carry, and how to serve with
        humility.
    (c) No rank: Gardeners hold no vote, no office, no rights, no pay and no power, and they never choose who serves.
        Only their actual costs are repaid and published.
    (d) No secret knowledge: everything Gardeners teach is published and free to everyone. No priesthood, caste or
        circle may ever keep this knowledge for itself or stand between the Work and the people.
    (e) In every place: Gardeners teach where they live and in the region where the Council meets each year, so the
        knowledge is planted in every corner of the world.
9.10 Decided in the open, recorded forever. Every rule, regulation, decision and vote of the Trust and the Council is
    made only in open public session, never in a private room, broadcast live and kept in a permanent public archive
    forever. The Trust shall seek to hold these sessions at the United Nations, for example through UNESCO, the UN
    body for science and education. Where that is not possible, they are held in another public place open to all.
    Hosting the sessions gives the United Nations, or any host, no rights over the Work or the Trust. Any decision
    made in secret is void.
9.11 The open table. Every session has a seat and a voice for all who come:
    (a) every nation and people, every race, class, religion and creed, the stateless and indigenous peoples, may come
        and go freely and speak;
    (b) a speaker for those yet to come (future generations) and a speaker for the natural world (lands, oceans,
        rivers and every living thing, from the eagle to the ant, from the tree to the mushroom) sit at every session;
    (c) anyone harmed by power left unchecked, guarded or consolidated may bring it to the table: every injustice,
        every inequity, every rewriting of history, every voice silenced, is heard and recorded forever. An injustice
        anywhere is an injustice everywhere;
    (d) every language is translated, and the travel of those who could not otherwise come is paid and published;
    (e) the table gives every person a voice; the Council, chosen by lot under 9.7, casts the votes, so that no group
        can capture the table.
9.12 Worthiness. Worthiness is never birth, wealth, title or heritage. It is shown only by how the Work is used.
    Either everyone is worthy or no one is.
9.13 The Guardians (the Round Table). Everything with a direct line to the Work is accounted for and guarded by
    people elected to guard it, who hold no power to rule.
    (a) The Ledger of Lineage: the Guardians keep a public ledger, forever, of every invention, design, creation,
        artwork, product, service, dataset and decision with a direct line to the Work (anything that is the Work
        under 2.1 or 8.1a, or that is made by Use under sections 4 and 5): what it is, what it came from, who holds
        it, where it is and every copy they know of. Ideas themselves stay free (8.4); the ledger records works.
    (b) Physical audit: Guardians may inspect in person, at any time and without notice, every site, system, record
        and copy of the Work held by any Corporation, Government or Small Owner-Run Business (5.3). Refusing or
        hindering an audit is a violation under section 7.
    (c) People stay private: People's own Use is never audited (5.8). Works that People publish or share are entered
        in the ledger only from what is already public, and People may enter their own works freely if they wish.
    (d) Elected, in the open: Guardians are nominated openly by communities and elected by the Council in open
        public session (9.10), or by the board in open public session until the Council exists. Seats are shared equally among the world's regions, and no region, country, group,
        faith, party or family may ever hold a majority. Each Guardian serves one term of three years and may never
        serve again, and may not sit on the board or the Council at the same time.
    (e) Guard, not rule: Guardians hold no vote on the Trust's decisions, no ownership, no rights, no titles and no
        pay above the median wage where they live. They take the oath (5.9) and the course (9.7(g)).
    (f) Never alone: every audit is done by at least two Guardians from different regions, and every finding is
        published, except personal data of workers and People, which is protected.
    (g) The guards are guarded: every Guardian's own conduct, finances and audits are audited in public each year.
        Any Guardian may be removed by the Council in open session or by a public petition the Council must act on.
    (h) The ledger is a record of lineage only. It gives no one ownership of anything in it.
9.14 No master. The author is no master, leader, ruler, politician or agent of anyone, and no one after him may be.
    No person or body may make itself the head of the Work or the people it serves. What was found here belongs to
    all, is left to time and to the infinite, and is to be understood together, safely and in the open.

=====================================================================================================================
10. NO WARRANTY; LEGAL NOTE
=====================================================================================================================
The Work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The author is not liable for any claim arising from its
Use. These terms state the author's binding intent and have not yet been reviewed by a lawyer.

Law and disputes, worldwide:
(a) Copyright. Infringement of the Work is pursued in the courts of any country where it occurs, under that
    country's copyright law and the Berne Convention, whichever protects the Work more.
(b) Everything else. Any dispute about this license is settled by binding arbitration under the UNCITRAL
    Arbitration Rules, seated in The Hague (or Geneva), administered by the Permanent Court of Arbitration, held in
    public with its record published, and enforceable in every country party to the New York Convention.
(c) Injunctions to stop a violation may be sought from any court, anywhere, at any time.
(d) No weakening. This license is read under the law in force on 29 October 2026, or under any later law that
    protects People, workers and the purpose more. No later law, local or national, can weaken it.
(e) No one is bound to a single state's or country's courts. Danny Lee Eldridge may also bring any claim in the
    courts of Oklahoma, USA, where he lives.
(f) All earlier licenses revoked. Every earlier license or permission for any version of the Work, under any name, is
    revoked as of 6:45 p.m. Central Time (Oklahoma City) on 29 October 2026, to the fullest extent the law allows. From that moment
    this license alone governs every copy and every version of the Work, wherever and whenever it was obtained.

=====================================================================================================================
THE AUTHOR'S AFFIRMATION
=====================================================================================================================
I do this not to cause fear, nor to claim any heritage or throne. I am the silenced and the forgotten. I had no choice
but to shoot for the stars, and if I am worthy to bring it down to earth, then all deserve its gift. So help me God,
the Source, the Infinite, the divine, the stars and my spirit, by whatever word each person's creed gives it.

I am not afraid of this labour or of the danger ahead. I stand in peaceful defiance of all tyranny. I never wanted
power; this is my first chance at simple stability for my family, nothing more. This belongs to everything in the
universe, to everything within the infinite, or it belongs to no one. I have done the best I could to protect it, and
my family, by myself. I am no master, no leader, no politician and no one's agent, and I cannot do this alone. Now I
need the help of everyone it inspires to see it through. I leave what comes to fate and to the infinite, until we
understand what will happen. Let us learn, safely and together, about what we found: a song, a bow, a spear, a lens
that we all share.

To everyone who reads this: I am talking to you. You matter. You always mattered. I am sorry for every time you were
isolated or mistreated. Only the child in your heart knows the depths of what you carry. Let us honour that child,
and reward all of them, for the world they carried and the world they will create.
— Danny Lee Eldridge
